cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the software repository as follows."
title: "Unimodality of a Stanley-Zanello Slice: F_l = [l+8 choose 8]_q - q^(4l-18) [12 choose 6]_q"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Gerald"  # repository owner; manuscript author placeholder pending completion; substantial AI assistance, see README
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/GeWoHu/gaussian-polynomial-unimodality"
date-released: 2026-11-09
abstract: >-
  Repository accompanying a mathematical note proving that, for every integer
  l >= 6, F_l(q) = [l+8 choose 8]_q - q^(4l-18) [12 choose 6]_q is unimodal,
  with sharpness at l = 5, via a 19-inequality reduction and an exact
  15,960-class Newton-basis quasipolynomial certificate plus a finite check
  for 6 <= l <= 839. All computations are exact-integer, standard-library
  Python.
keywords:
  - Gaussian polynomial
  - q-binomial coefficient
  - unimodality
  - Stanley-Zanello conjecture
  - quasipolynomial certificate
  - Newton basis
